WEBVTT

00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:34.368
In what has become a winter tradition,

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:37.037
members of the Zarlon Seven
Polar Bear Club

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.123
today took the plunge
into a river of liquid ammonia.

00:00:43.919 --> 00:00:45.754
There were no survivors.

00:00:47.464 --> 00:00:49.091
Takes all kinds.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:51.802
And now, with his annual Xmas message,

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.388
here's the head
of the Xmas Safety Council,

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:56.265
the Head of Walter Cronkite.

00:00:56.557 --> 00:00:59.184
Season's Warnings, Linda and Morbo.

00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:02.229
This guy's too trustworthy.
What's his angle?

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:06.191
In all the tinsel and terror
of the holiday season,

00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:09.611
we too often underestimate
that murderous brute,

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:12.030
better known as Santa Claus.

00:01:12.114 --> 00:01:15.367
With images
of last year's Gingerbread Massacre

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.870
freshly baked into our memories,

00:01:17.953 --> 00:01:22.583
I remind you to bolt your doors,
say goodbye to your pets,

00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:25.043
and lock your children in the closet.

00:01:25.377 --> 00:01:28.922
This is Walter Cronkite saying,
"I told you so."

00:01:33.385 --> 00:01:36.096
Sacred Boar of Western and Eastern Samoa,

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.848
we've got to secure for Santa's arrival.

00:01:38.891 --> 00:01:41.685
Just as well.
I'm getting tired of this wood show.

00:01:44.188 --> 00:01:46.356
Cover that fireplace, confound you.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:50.152
I've only a few years to live.
I don't wanna spend them dead.

00:01:50.277 --> 00:01:52.487
We're pushing as hard as we can.

00:01:52.571 --> 00:01:54.448
Oh, pushing.

00:01:57.075 --> 00:02:00.120
Oh, we're doomed. Every year we're doomed.

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:03.707
Thanks be I had these
bulletproof shutters installed.

00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:15.093
Bring it on, Santa.

00:02:15.302 --> 00:02:18.430
That bloodthirsty
cadaver junkie can't touch us

00:02:18.514 --> 00:02:21.266
as long as we're not stupid enough
to leave this building.

00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:22.476
- Good!
- All right!

00:02:23.769 --> 00:02:26.104
In a related matter,
you'll be delivering

00:02:26.522 --> 00:02:29.316
this sack of children's letters
directly to Santa

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:31.527
at his Death Fortress on Neptune.

00:02:44.039 --> 00:02:47.000
These letters are real butt nutters.
Listen to this one.

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:48.335
"Dear Santa..."

00:02:48.669 --> 00:02:51.380
Please, please don't bring me any gifts.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.716
The bicycle you fired at me
last year from your bicycle gun

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.677
really tore up my insides.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.971
Awful. Let's read some more.

00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:00.389
"Dear Santa..."

00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:02.891
Please bring me a coffin for Grandpa.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.227
You choked him with a chestnut last year,

00:03:05.394 --> 00:03:09.189
and he's beginning to smell
a lot like Xmas, if you know what I mean.

00:03:11.608 --> 00:03:12.734
It's not fair.

00:03:12.818 --> 00:03:16.572
In my day, Xmas was supposed to bring
people together, not blow them apart.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:21.201
Sure, but who’s gonna do anything
about it? Certainly not us, no sir.

00:03:21.285 --> 00:03:23.078
Certainly yes us, uh-huh, sir.

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:26.331
We've gotta bring back
the kind of Xmas I remember.

00:03:26.582 --> 00:03:27.708
Fry's right.

00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:31.003
It's time to sit on Santa's lap, and hard.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:48.979
Oh, look, a cute little welcoming party.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.901
Hey, wanna buy a tiny little kidney?

00:03:53.984 --> 00:03:55.444
I'll let you punch me for a buck.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.031
Uh, look, we've got mail for Santa.
Are you his elves?

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:00.824
We're not elves. We're Neptunians.

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:03.202
We're just shrimpy
because he doesn't feed us.

00:04:04.453 --> 00:04:06.163
You hit me. You owe me a dollar.

00:04:13.837 --> 00:04:18.425
Help. You got any food,
old tea bags, chewed gum, apple cores?

00:04:18.509 --> 00:04:20.052
Come on, we're starving here.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.929
But you live in a gingerbread house.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.097
Hey, it's food or shelter, not both.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:28.018
You lazy runts.
Don't you get paid for making the toys?

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.353
- Who said toys?
- Toys?

00:04:29.436 --> 00:04:30.854
- You said toys?
- What did they say?

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.606
False alarm, folks.

00:04:32.898 --> 00:04:36.109
There's no reason to make toys
since Santa judges everyone to be naughty.

00:04:38.153 --> 00:04:42.074
That's it. I'm gonna deliver
a gift of my boot up Santa's chimney.

00:04:42.241 --> 00:04:45.327
- Where is he?
- There, in his ice fortress.

00:04:50.874 --> 00:04:53.210
We'll need help getting in.
Any volunteers?

00:04:57.381 --> 00:04:58.507
I'll help you.

00:04:59.049 --> 00:05:00.050
Ah, phooey.

00:05:19.611 --> 00:05:21.238
- An omen?
- Dinner.

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:32.499
Let's see who’s been naughty
and who’s been naughty.

00:05:34.877 --> 00:05:38.714
Mobsters beating up a shopkeeper
for protection money.

00:05:39.131 --> 00:05:40.883
Very naughty.

00:05:41.675 --> 00:05:44.553
Shopkeeper's not paying
the protection money.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:47.097
Exactly as naughty.

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:51.602
I saw that.

00:05:52.936 --> 00:05:53.937
Huh?

00:05:54.521 --> 00:05:55.647
We brought your mail.

00:05:56.648 --> 00:06:01.111
Don't you ever knock? Who knows
what naughty things I could be watching.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.488
I get New Orleans on this thing, you know?

00:06:03.572 --> 00:06:04.656
Don't kill us.

00:06:06.742 --> 00:06:08.035
Santa's a robot.

00:06:08.118 --> 00:06:11.496
So we should be able to destroy him
with a logical paradox.

00:06:11.663 --> 00:06:13.457
Bender, you'd better cover your ears.

00:06:15.542 --> 00:06:18.045
Holy night! Intruders!

00:06:19.546 --> 00:06:20.714
Hold it, Santa.

00:06:23.008 --> 00:06:26.094
Consider this, you are programmed
to destroy the naughty.

00:06:26.845 --> 00:06:29.598
But many of those you destroy
are, in fact, nice.

00:06:29.973 --> 00:06:32.434
I submit to you that you are naughty,

00:06:32.518 --> 00:06:35.270
and that logically
you must destroy yourself.

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:48.992
Nice try, but my head was built
with paradox-absorbing crumple zones.

00:07:11.723 --> 00:07:13.934
Wait. This is what we're running from.

00:07:19.273 --> 00:07:20.482
Faster. Faster.

00:07:23.527 --> 00:07:24.528
Whoa!

00:07:45.007 --> 00:07:46.508
Why aren't we moving?

00:07:46.592 --> 00:07:47.718
I don't know.

00:07:47.801 --> 00:07:50.762
Usually when I do stuff like this,
the ship moves.

00:07:54.641 --> 00:07:55.642
Ho, ho.

00:08:06.445 --> 00:08:07.446
He's trapped.

00:08:07.613 --> 00:08:08.614
Hooray!

00:08:10.616 --> 00:08:12.409
Now we can make toys again.

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:15.412
Toys! Toys! Toys!

00:08:15.621 --> 00:08:18.999
And I can deliver them.
Billions and billions in one night.

00:08:19.166 --> 00:08:21.919
Ha! No human could do all that.

00:08:22.044 --> 00:08:23.337
Evel Knievel could.

00:08:23.587 --> 00:08:24.588
Nuh-uh.

00:08:24.838 --> 00:08:27.299
Santa's right. We need some sort of robot.

00:08:29.718 --> 00:08:32.221
Ah, crap. I'm some sort of robot.

00:08:34.223 --> 00:08:35.224
Hooray!

00:08:35.933 --> 00:08:36.934
Hooray!

00:08:37.851 --> 00:08:38.852
Hooray!

00:08:44.191 --> 00:08:49.321
Bender can't be Santa. He wasn't built
to yuletide specifications.

00:08:49.488 --> 00:08:52.824
Oh, yeah? Well, I wasn't built
to steal Leela's purse either,

00:08:52.908 --> 00:08:54.326
but that didn't stop me.

00:08:54.451 --> 00:08:57.913
- Bender.
- Bow before your new Santa.

00:08:58.205 --> 00:08:59.665
Our hero.

00:09:00.582 --> 00:09:04.461
We are free and fairly sober
With so many toys to build

00:09:04.837 --> 00:09:06.797
The machines are kind of tricky

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:11.009
Probably someone will be killed
But we gladly work for nothing

00:09:11.218 --> 00:09:14.805
Which is good
Because we don't intend to pay

00:09:16.348 --> 00:09:19.810
The elves are back to work today,
Hooray!

00:09:21.979 --> 00:09:24.106
We have just a couple hours

00:09:24.231 --> 00:09:28.360
To make several billion gifts
And the labor isn't easy

00:09:28.443 --> 00:09:30.362
Then you'll all work triple shifts

00:09:30.529 --> 00:09:32.614
You can make the job go quicker

00:09:32.698 --> 00:09:35.784
If you turn up the controls
To super speed

00:09:37.202 --> 00:09:39.329
It's back to work on Xmas eve

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:40.831
Hooray!

00:09:41.331 --> 00:09:44.793
And though you're cold
And sore and ugly

00:09:44.877 --> 00:09:47.629
Your pride will mask the pain

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:51.258
Let my happy smile warm your hearts

00:09:51.341 --> 00:09:54.261
There's a toy lodged in my brain

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:58.182
We are getting awfully tired
And we can't work any faster

00:09:58.265 --> 00:10:00.017
And we're very, very sorry

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.518
Why, you selfish little bastards

00:10:01.602 --> 00:10:03.312
Do you want the kids to think

00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:05.981
That Santa's just a crummy
Empty-handed jerk?

00:10:06.231 --> 00:10:07.232
- Ow!
- Sorry.

00:10:07.482 --> 00:10:09.526
Then shut your yaps and back to work

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:15.574
Now it's very nearly Xmas
And we've done the best we could

00:10:15.657 --> 00:10:17.367
These toy soldiers are poorly painted

00:10:17.451 --> 00:10:18.911
And they're made from inferior wood

00:10:19.077 --> 00:10:22.497
I should give you all a beating
But I really have to fly

00:10:22.581 --> 00:10:25.876
If I weren't stuck here frozen
I'd harpoon you in the eye

00:10:25.959 --> 00:10:29.671
Now it's back into our tenements
To drown ourselves in rye

00:10:29.838 --> 00:10:33.759
You did the best you could, I guess
And some of these gorillas are okay

00:10:33.884 --> 00:10:35.427
We're adequate.

00:10:35.511 --> 00:10:38.847
The elves have rescued Xmas day!
Hooray!

00:10:56.448 --> 00:10:58.867
Gee, Bender,
how are you gonna get through these bars?

00:10:59.076 --> 00:11:01.620
I don't know, moron. Suppose I bend 'em?

00:11:01.995 --> 00:11:02.996
Okay.

00:11:04.248 --> 00:11:05.249
Ow!

00:11:05.332 --> 00:11:08.001
Mommy, Mommy.
Santa's through the perimeter.

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:11.630
This is it, kids. Take your suicide pills
so you won't suffer.

00:11:11.839 --> 00:11:14.049
No, wait. I'm the good Santa.

00:11:14.132 --> 00:11:16.969
I've got toys. At very reasonable prices.

00:11:17.177 --> 00:11:20.848
Don't listen to him. He's the father
of all lies, and the uncle of all tricks.

00:11:21.098 --> 00:11:23.100
But I come bearing Tri-Ominos.

00:11:23.267 --> 00:11:24.393
Go for the shins!

00:11:24.518 --> 00:11:25.519
Ahh!

00:11:26.520 --> 00:11:27.521
Ow, ow, ow!

00:11:30.691 --> 00:11:31.692
Oh...

00:11:32.734 --> 00:11:34.111
One down.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:43.328
Well, hello there, handsome.

00:11:43.537 --> 00:11:45.581
Won't ya have a cookie?

00:11:46.707 --> 00:11:48.250
Don't mind if I do.

00:11:48.709 --> 00:11:49.751
Ow!

00:11:49.877 --> 00:11:51.003
Ow! What's in these things?

00:11:51.086 --> 00:11:54.339
Why don't you slip into something
more fiery.

00:11:55.507 --> 00:11:58.886
Ahh! Whoa! Ow!

00:12:03.557 --> 00:12:04.558
Ow.

00:12:08.103 --> 00:12:10.522
Yo, Kringle. What happened to you, dog?

00:12:10.606 --> 00:12:14.026
Oh, it's awful, Kwanza-Bot.
Everyone hates me.

00:12:14.818 --> 00:12:16.987
At least they understand you,
you know what I'm sayin'?

00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:18.947
Ain't nobody down with this Kwanza tiff.

00:12:19.114 --> 00:12:21.909
Hey, maybe you can lend me a hand
with these deliveries?

00:12:22.701 --> 00:12:25.954
No time. I gotta hand out
the traditional Kwanza Book.

00:12:29.041 --> 00:12:32.085
I've been giving these out for 647 years.

00:12:42.012 --> 00:12:45.682
Ah, bathtub eggnog,
just the way Grandma used to drink.

00:12:47.559 --> 00:12:49.645
Ew! It went sour.

00:12:50.062 --> 00:12:52.439
Can't I have a scented bath in peace?

00:12:53.273 --> 00:12:56.318
Remember, Professor. Bender is Santa.

00:12:56.527 --> 00:12:58.237
So we don't need to hurt him, right?

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:01.573
Yes, yes, yes.
You sound like a broken mp3.

00:13:02.741 --> 00:13:03.784
Ho, ho...

00:13:03.951 --> 00:13:04.952
Ow!

00:13:05.035 --> 00:13:08.205
Professor, don't you remember
what I told you?

00:13:08.288 --> 00:13:09.623
No!

00:13:11.166 --> 00:13:12.167
Oh...

00:13:14.586 --> 00:13:17.631
Oh, there's got to be a better way.

00:13:22.511 --> 00:13:24.972
Bender, you’re a genius.

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:30.269
This creates an unrealistic
standard of beauty.

00:13:30.727 --> 00:13:34.147
Now it's time for Santa
to screw open his present.

00:13:37.818 --> 00:13:39.528
It's Santa. And we got him cornered.

00:13:39.611 --> 00:13:42.406
Oh, I smell a juicy promotion for me.

00:13:42.489 --> 00:13:44.950
And a juicy re-hiring
back onto the force for me.

00:13:45.117 --> 00:13:47.536
Ah, Wh-What?

00:13:53.876 --> 00:13:56.920
This Xmas day session of court
will come to order.

00:13:57.171 --> 00:13:59.381
The Honorable Judge Whitey presiding.

00:14:01.091 --> 00:14:06.555
Santa Claus, you stand accused of crimes
against humanity. How do you plead?

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:08.974
- Not Santa.
- There he is again.

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:16.023
Now Pramala, I know it's scary
in that there witness box,

00:14:16.106 --> 00:14:18.859
but 'taint no need to fear me.

00:14:20.652 --> 00:14:22.905
I'm sorry. I thought you was corn.

00:14:23.447 --> 00:14:27.159
Now, would you please point
at that robot over there?

00:14:30.204 --> 00:14:31.830
No further questions.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:37.794
Daddy done good, huh?

00:14:38.212 --> 00:14:42.007
Isn't it true that you have been paid
for your testimony?

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:44.676
Yes. You gave me a dollar and some candy.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:47.679
And yet you haven't said
what I told you to say.

00:14:47.763 --> 00:14:49.431
How can any of us trust you?

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:53.644
Quit badgering the witness.

00:14:53.727 --> 00:14:55.020
Badger? Where?

00:14:57.856 --> 00:15:02.986
Whereas I have a ham dinner with
mayonnaise waiting for me at my mansion,

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:04.905
I find the defendant guilty.

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:11.703
Santa Claus, I hereby sentence you
to be executed at sundown.

00:15:13.664 --> 00:15:17.751
It's not fair. I just hope
that dumb chicken is ashamed of himself.

00:15:27.386 --> 00:15:31.932
Deactivated robot walking.
We got a deactivated robot walking here.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:38.438
Hey, Santa, when you see the Robot Devil,
tell him I'm a-comin'.

00:15:40.858 --> 00:15:43.652
- Hey, that guy said to tell you that...
- I heard him.

00:15:53.954 --> 00:15:57.749
Greetings, masters.
My companion and I made lots of toys.

00:15:57.875 --> 00:15:59.251
Out of my way, shrimp-o.

00:15:59.334 --> 00:16:02.504
We're here to bring Santa back
so we can prove Bender's innocent.

00:16:06.884 --> 00:16:10.512
Do what you will,
but we'll see who has the last "Ho."

00:16:14.558 --> 00:16:17.102
- There.
- Oh no. The ice is melting.

00:16:17.269 --> 00:16:20.564
The pollution from the factory.
It caused a greenhouse effect.

00:16:20.647 --> 00:16:22.024
That would explain this heat.

00:16:22.107 --> 00:16:23.650
And your breezy short shorts.

00:16:23.775 --> 00:16:25.485
Uh, yeah, that would explain it.

00:16:54.515 --> 00:16:55.516
Oh!

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:04.858
Hurry. We've got to think of another way
to save Bender, or Xmas will be ruined.

00:17:04.942 --> 00:17:06.401
Especially for Bender.

00:17:10.989 --> 00:17:12.366
Look out, Earth.

00:17:12.741 --> 00:17:16.537
I'm dreaming of a red Xmas.

00:17:25.379 --> 00:17:27.089
Ah, good old Maggie.

00:17:29.216 --> 00:17:30.300
When I pull the switch,

00:17:30.384 --> 00:17:33.470
these powerful electromagnets
will tear you limb from limb,

00:17:33.554 --> 00:17:35.514
killing you
in the most humane possible manner.

00:17:35.681 --> 00:17:38.725
But Mr. Mayor, that doesn't sound humane.

00:17:38.934 --> 00:17:41.478
It is for the witnesses
because it's not boring.

00:17:45.941 --> 00:17:50.529
The instant this random number generator
reaches zero, you'll be executed.

00:17:50.696 --> 00:17:51.697
Oh.

00:17:53.073 --> 00:17:55.075
Ten. Three.

00:17:55.993 --> 00:17:57.035
Twelve.

00:17:57.619 --> 00:17:59.872
- Three again.
- Stop the execution.

00:17:59.997 --> 00:18:01.623
- Leela.
- Fifteen.

00:18:01.957 --> 00:18:04.209
- Negative eight.
- You've got the wrong Santa.

00:18:04.293 --> 00:18:05.335
And I'll prove it.

00:18:05.502 --> 00:18:06.837
I'm Santa Claus.

00:18:08.005 --> 00:18:09.339
What? Twenty-seven.

00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:11.383
No. I'm Santa Claus.

00:18:11.717 --> 00:18:14.386
- Six?
- We're also Santa Claus.

00:18:14.595 --> 00:18:16.597
And I'm his friend, Jesus.

00:18:16.722 --> 00:18:20.684
Your Mayor-ness, if you execute him,
you have to execute all of us.

00:18:21.018 --> 00:18:24.146
You people aren't Santa.
You're not even robots.

00:18:24.271 --> 00:18:27.941
Ninety-one.
How dare you lie in front of Jesus?

00:18:28.192 --> 00:18:29.318
Hey. Zero.

00:18:32.571 --> 00:18:33.989
No. Stop the magnet.

00:18:34.698 --> 00:18:39.953
Swing low, sweet chariot

00:18:40.162 --> 00:18:43.457
Comin' for to carry me home

00:18:43.916 --> 00:18:45.250
Swing low

00:18:45.334 --> 00:18:46.335
This is horrible.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:47.920
But it's not boring.

00:18:49.796 --> 00:18:51.590
Ho, ho, ho.

00:18:57.763 --> 00:19:00.474
My God, the real Santa. Get him, Jesus!

00:19:00.599 --> 00:19:02.476
I help those who help themselves.

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:08.273
Santa, you saved my life.
Please don't kill me.

00:19:10.442 --> 00:19:12.402
I'm not here to kill you, Bender.

00:19:12.694 --> 00:19:15.781
I need you to help me save Xmas.

00:19:17.741 --> 00:19:19.451
Gee whiz, Santa.

00:19:19.826 --> 00:19:21.912
You want me to help you?

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:23.664
Don't do it. He's evil.

00:19:23.789 --> 00:19:26.124
I know he is, but I have no choice.

00:19:26.375 --> 00:19:30.504
I'm running late,
and if I don't complete my brutal rampage,

00:19:30.587 --> 00:19:33.340
well, it just wouldn't be Xmas.

00:19:33.674 --> 00:19:35.175
I guess what I'm asking is,

00:19:35.551 --> 00:19:39.346
Bender, won't you join my slaying tonight?

00:19:39.596 --> 00:19:40.681
Well...

00:19:40.931 --> 00:19:42.182
'Tis the season.

00:20:04.788 --> 00:20:05.831
My hair!

00:20:05.914 --> 00:20:07.457
My wedding cake!

00:20:08.709 --> 00:20:10.085
Let it snow.

00:20:12.462 --> 00:20:14.381
Merry Xmas, kids.

00:20:19.386 --> 00:20:20.387
Ahh!

00:20:26.101 --> 00:20:27.519
This wangs chung.

00:20:27.603 --> 00:20:31.023
After all the good we tried to do,
Xmas turned out as rotten as ever.

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:33.066
- No heat.
- No power.

00:20:33.233 --> 00:20:36.612
Huddled together in fear
like lice in a burning wig.

00:20:37.196 --> 00:20:40.991
Wait a second. Maybe your futuristic Xmas
isn't so rotten after all.

00:20:41.158 --> 00:20:44.453
What are you talking about, you crouton?
You said it yourself.

00:20:44.745 --> 00:20:48.415
Xmas should be about bringing people
together, not blowing them apart.

00:20:48.582 --> 00:20:51.502
But don't you see?
Fear has brought us together.

00:20:51.668 --> 00:20:53.378
That's the magic of Xmas.

00:20:53.545 --> 00:20:54.838
That's a big crock of...

00:20:56.423 --> 00:20:57.424
Hold me.

00:21:05.849 --> 00:21:08.602
On, Trasher! On, Smasher!

00:21:09.269 --> 00:21:11.313
Hey, Kwanza-Bot. Where you off to?

00:21:11.522 --> 00:21:12.689
You didn't hear about it?

00:21:12.773 --> 00:21:15.943
Chanukah Zombie's having a luau
at the B’nai Brith. You coming?

00:21:16.026 --> 00:21:17.027
Word.

00:21:19.363 --> 00:21:22.533
By the way, Bender,
here's a small token of my appreciation

00:21:22.616 --> 00:21:25.202
for being Santa
while I was trapped in the ice.

00:21:25.452 --> 00:21:26.453
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo.

00:21:28.038 --> 00:21:30.666
Hey, chief, you screwed up.
There's nothing in here.

00:21:30.874 --> 00:21:34.628
Oh, it might appear empty,
but the message is clear.

00:21:34.711 --> 00:21:39.842
Play Santa again
and I'll kill you next year.

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:41.927
Ahhh!

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:49.643
Ho, ho, ho.